where he was found selling Khoa, a food articles meant for sale for human consumption ;
- that FI disclosed his identity and expressed his intention to purchase a sample of Yellow Chilly Powder from the vendor, to which he agreed ;
- that thereafter as per the prescribed procedure under the PFA Act and Rules after giving notice to the vendor and offer towards sale price of sample to which he refused to accept, sample was then lifted ; that sample was separately packed, fastened, marked, sealed and necessary documents including Notice as per Form-VI in the presence of appellant/accused, panchnama etc was prepared at the spot ; that thereafter one counterpart of sample was sent to Public Analyst (PA) in intact condition and other two counterparts were deposited with SDM/LHA ;
- that vide report dated 22.11.1999, PA found the sample to be not conforming to the standards on the ground that milk fat on dried weight basis was 27.66% which was less than the prescribed minimum limit of 30% ;
- that upon receipt of report, SDM/LHA directed investigation which was carried out by FI and after completion of investigation sanction under Section 20 of the PFA Act was obtained from the Director PFA.

APPEAL : Partly allowed;partly dismissed Decision : Conviction upheld;
Gopi Singh vs Delhi Administration/ on 6 October, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/145950077/
